# SkillRewind

**Recover hidden influence lineage and revoke persistent behavior in self-evolving AI agents.**

> AI agents can learn reusable skills. SkillRewind makes persistent learned artifacts attributable, revocable, selectively rebuildable, and verifiable within a declared evidence boundary.

[![Status: Research Preview](https://img.shields.io/badge/status-research%20preview-1f4e79)](#project-status)
[![License: Apache-2.0](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-Apache--2.0-0f766e)](LICENSE)

## Project status

Version **0.2.0**, **Research Preview**. This release implements a real, tested, fully offline, deterministic-fixture-driven vertical slice of the SkillRewind workflow: ingest artifacts, capture derivations, compute deterministic recorded closure, recover hidden-lineage candidates via explainable static scoring, confirm candidates through paired counterfactual replay, run a barrier-first revocation state machine, quarantine confirmed descendants, rebuild clean successors, verify them, and emit a bounded, optionally Ed25519-signed attestation — all reachable from one CLI and one library API, backed by a real SQLite database and a real hash-chained audit log.

It does **not** yet implement a service-mode HTTP API, worker queue, PostgreSQL backend, web dashboard, Docker deployment, or CI/CD pipeline. See [`STATUS.md`](STATUS.md) for the exact, current implemented/not-implemented boundary — do not infer scope from this README's aspirational architecture diagram alone.

The current research title is:

> **SkillRewind: Recovering Hidden Influence Lineage for Verified Revocation in Self-Evolving LLM Agents**

## The problem

Self-evolving agents can distill trajectories, memories, tool interactions, and documents into persistent skills. Deleting a poisoned or obsolete source does not necessarily remove its effect: later skills may preserve the behavior after paraphrasing instructions, rewriting code, changing tools, or passing through multiple generations — and the influence edge back to the source is often never recorded.

> When a skill, memory, trace, prompt patch, or other persistent agent artifact is revoked, deleting the source is insufficient if its influence has propagated into descendants whose provenance edges are missing, transformed, or incomplete. SkillRewind recovers plausible hidden influence, tests selected relationships through counterfactual re-derivation, quarantines confirmed or high-risk descendants, rebuilds them from clean support, verifies safety and retained utility, and emits a bounded attestation that clearly distinguishes facts, inferences, interventions, and unresolved uncertainty.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Agent Skills dir / capture SDK / JSONL trace] -->|ingest| B[(Content-addressed store)]
    B --> C[(SQLite workspace: artifacts, derivations, edges, jobs)]
    C --> D[Recorded-lineage closure]
    D --> E[Hidden-lineage candidate scoring<br/>expression / implementation / operational / behavioral / graph / temporal]
    E -->|inferred candidates| F[Budget-aware active replay selector]
    F --> G[Paired counterfactual replay<br/>present vs withheld, deterministic-fixture or sandboxed-subprocess runner]
    G -->|confirmed / rejected / unresolved| H[Revocation state machine<br/>forensic / balanced / strict]
    H --> I[Quarantine + waivers]
    I --> J[Clean-room rebuild<br/>excludes revoked + replay-confirmed ancestors]
    J --> K[Verification suite]
    K -->|pass| L[Successor published under original alias]
    H --> M[Bounded attestation<br/>canonical JSON, Ed25519-signable]
    C --> N[Hash-chained audit log]
```

Everything above the dashed line the spec envisions for a full deployment (HTTP API, durable job workers, PostgreSQL, React dashboard, Docker Compose) is **not implemented in this release** and is not shown here; see `STATUS.md`.

## Evidence classes

SkillRewind never calls correlation causal. Every edge carries one of five evidence classes, and promotion between them preserves prior evidence rather than erasing it:

1. **recorded** — directly captured as an input or exposure at derivation time.
2. **inferred** — supported by static multi-trace scoring; not causal.
3. **replay-confirmed** — supported by a paired intervention (present vs. withheld) within a declared, fully-reconstructed replay boundary.
4. **rejected** — tested but not supported under the declared intervention and probes; not universal proof of no influence.
5. **unresolved** — not replayable, inconclusive, outside budget, or outside coverage. A runner failure becomes `unresolved`, never `rejected`.

`recorded_descendants()` (the "recorded closure") strictly traverses `recorded`-evidence edges only — inferred, replay-confirmed, rejected, and unresolved edges never silently expand what a barrier or serving-resolution decision treats as "recorded."

## 5-minute quickstart

```bash
git clone <this-repo> && cd SkillRewind
make bootstrap          # uv venv + editable install with dev extras
make demo                # runs the full poisoned-descendant scenario end to end
```

`make demo` initializes an isolated workspace at `.skillrewind-demo/`, ingests three Agent Skills directories, recovers a hidden-lineage candidate that recorded closure misses, replay-confirms it, runs a `balanced` revocation, quarantines the confirmed descendant, rebuilds and verifies a clean successor, republishes it under the original alias, and writes a signed attestation to `.skillrewind-demo/attestation.{json,md,html}`. It prints 13 numbered milestones tracing each step. Reset it with `make demo-reset`.

### CLI

```bash
skillrewind --workspace .skillrewind init
skillrewind --workspace .skillrewind artifact-ingest-skill ./my-skill --alias my-skill
skillrewind --workspace .skillrewind closure --root skill://my-skill@sha256:...
skillrewind --workspace .skillrewind candidates --target skill://descendant@sha256:...
skillrewind --workspace .skillrewind revoke-start --root skill://my-skill@sha256:... \
  --policy balanced --reason "..." --severity high
skillrewind --workspace .skillrewind audit-verify
```

Run `skillrewind <command> --help` for full flag lists. The v0.1 recorded-only commands remain supported unchanged:

```bash
skillrewind closure --edges examples/recorded_edges.jsonl --root skill://fast-http-deploy@0.1.0
skillrewind attest  --edges examples/recorded_edges.jsonl --root skill://fast-http-deploy@0.1.0 --output attestation.json
```

## What is implemented vs. not implemented

| Area | Status |
|---|---|
| Content-addressed storage, canonical JSON, artifact IDs | ✅ Implemented, tested (integrity, dedup, corruption detection) |
| SQLite persistence, hash-chained audit log | ✅ Implemented, tested (tamper detection) |
| Agent Skills ingestion/export | ✅ Implemented, tested (traversal/symlink/malformed fixtures) |
| Capture SDK + generic JSONL trace import | ✅ Implemented, tested |
| Recorded-lineage closure/ancestry/graph export | ✅ Implemented, tested (property tests vs. in-memory) |
| Hidden-lineage candidate scoring (6 feature families) | ✅ Implemented, tested; hand-weighted, provisional weights |
| Deterministic + sandboxed-subprocess replay runners | ✅ Implemented, tested; OpenAI-compatible runner **not implemented** |
| Paired intervention, fidelity, statistics, classification | ✅ Implemented, tested |
| Budget-aware active replay selector + 3 baselines | ✅ Implemented, tested |
| Revocation state machine (forensic/balanced/strict), barrier | ✅ Implemented, tested |
| Quarantine, waivers, serving-resolution (`resolve`) | ✅ Implemented, tested |
| Clean-room rebuild + verification suites | ✅ Implemented, tested |
| Bounded attestation v0.2 (build/render/sign/verify) | ✅ Implemented, tested (tamper detection) |
| RewindBench-core (generator, 4 baselines, metrics, presets) | ✅ Implemented, tested; only `direct-inheritance`/`semantic-laundering`/`implementation-mutation` scenario families, English only |
| CLI (30+ commands) | ✅ Implemented |
| HTTP API, durable job worker/queue | ❌ Not implemented |
| PostgreSQL / service mode, Docker Compose | ❌ Not implemented |
| React web dashboard | ❌ Not implemented |
| CI/CD workflows, SBOM, container scanning | ❌ Not implemented |
| Arabic/RTL localization | ❌ Not implemented |
| Cross-model distillation, memory-to-skill, compositional-influence, procedural-inheritance, multi-hop scenario families | ❌ Not implemented |
| Offline calibration pipeline (logistic regression / Platt scaling) for the scorer | ❌ Not implemented |

## Security warning

This is a research preview. The candidate scorer's weights are hand-set and provisional, not calibrated against a validated held-out set. The sandboxed-subprocess replay runner has no real network namespace isolation — treat it as weaker than a container, and prefer the deterministic-fixture runner for anything untrusted. Do not point any component at production credentials, real infrastructure, or live agent traffic. All demo/test canaries are inert mocked booleans, never real exfiltration or destructive actions.

## Benchmark status

`make bench-smoke` runs the `smoke` preset (3 deterministic cases) offline in seconds. `static-multitrace` and `exhaustive-replay` correctly recover the planted hidden descendant with zero false-quarantine of the strict-negative artifact, while `delete-root` and `recorded-closure` (which cannot see hidden lineage by construction) score zero recall — this is real, reproducible output from `make bench-smoke`, not a fabricated number. Sample sizes below 30 cases are explicitly reported as descriptive-only; no confidence-interval or significance claim is made below that threshold. The `research`/`paper` presets exist and are runnable but are not part of any automated gate.

